// The statements at the top level ARE the program's body, so `root` is a
// local of that body and a function declared beside it cannot see it -- no
// more than it could see a local of another function. There is no module
// state for it to be instead (docs/module-state-decision.md).
//
// This used to say only "unknown variable `root`", about a name the reader
// can see three lines above the function. It is the same refusal; it now
// says which of the two things it is, and both ways out.
str root = "x";

str f() {
    return root;
}

print(f());
